#: ../../development.rst:113 cb6829878c62428183f08272f754ca26
msgid ""
"**2 tests marked ``xfail``** "
"(``tests/test_fees.py::test_distritec_fees_simple_package``, "
"``test_distritec_fees_multiple_packages``, both ``strict=True``): the "
"expected totals don't match ``api/services/fees.py``'s current output. "
"Needs someone who knows the intended Distritec tariff to say which side "
"is wrong. ``strict=True`` means if the underlying bug ever gets fixed, "
"these flip to a hard test failure (``XPASS``) instead of silently staying"
" green -- remove the marker at that point, don't leave it in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../development.rst:120 08213cdde2a443bd91d048b51a10f3f7
msgid ""
"**mypy**: clean at its current (non-strict) level -- the ~32 findings "
"this surfaced when first turned on (mostly a ``dict[str, str]`` parameter"
" annotation that was actually ``dict[str, Any]`` in practice, since "
"Airtable fields aren't all strings, plus a few missing local annotations "
"and two untyped tariff-table dicts in ``api/services/fees.py``) have all "
"been fixed. ``--strict`` finds ~106 more, almost all missing-annotation "
"noise across the wider codebase rather than bugs -- a deliberate future "
"ratchet, not turned on yet."
msgstr ""

